    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24794" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">invītātor</span></b> ,
			ōris, m.
		invito, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>one who invites</i>, <i>an
			inviter</i> (<b>poet.</b> and post-class.), <i><span class="en">Mart. 3, 23</span></i>
			<i>lemm.;</i>
			<i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 9, 13</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Marc. 4, 25</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aeternae vitae invitator, Christus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib.</span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Esp., <i>the officer charged with invitations at the
				court</i>, Cod. 12, 60, 10; <i><span class="en">Inscr.
				Orell. 4436</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Caesaris, Jovis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					9, 91, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
